MID_SE_Ism_Max_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_001: Promised One, I've finished mending that banner.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_002: <NCA>"I'm sorry for giving you these odd jobs."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_003: No, don't mention it! I enjoy working with fabrics.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_004: Actually, there was a time—long ago, now—when I\napprenticed as a tailor.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_005: So if your clothes ever need attention, bring them\nto me. I'm happy to do it, really!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_006: I guess, uh...enjoying needlework doesn't make you\nan intimidating knight, does it?
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_007: <NCA>"You have other ways of being intimidating."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_008: <NCB>"You haven't always been knightly."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_009: <ACA>Huh? I don't know what you're talking\nabout. Unless...
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_010: <ACB>Huh? Wait. You don't mean...
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_011: Are you talking about him?
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_012: How do you know about me and Jester?!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_013: <NCA>"You have the same eyes."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_014: <NCB>"I see how you are in battle."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_015: I can't believe you saw through the disguise.\nThat's... Argh!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_016: You've known about that side of me all this time,\nand you didn't say anything?!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_017: I always thought if you knew about that, you\nwouldn't have taken me in.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_018: The Infernal Clown doesn't belong anywhere near\nthe Herald of the Pale Raven.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_019: <NCA>"It doesn't bother me."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_020: Alright, Promised One. I'm going to try to\nbelieve that.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_021: I'll serve you using all the skills I have, from fighting\nto mending clothes.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_022: For peace. For— Heh heh. PEACE!\nHeh heh HEH!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_023: <NCA>"That's all I ask."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_A_024: 
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_001: *sob* Please, please, come back.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_002: I've stood here in prayer for so long. I thought that\nwould be enough.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_003: Haha! You need another supplicant, huh? You\nneed ME!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_004: Heh heh HEH! You've been baaad, little lamb.\nCome back, before I rain blood on your grave!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_005: <NCA>"What are you doing?"
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_006: Oh! Promised One!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_007: You came back. Praying as him... I guess that was\nwhat it took!
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_008: I have something for you. I'm so glad I don't have to\njust leave it at your grave.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_009: <NCA>"What a beautiful cloak."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_010: <NCB>"So, you are good at needlework."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_011: <ACA>It's dyed the color of the sunrise, to signify the\ndawning peace we've achieved.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_012: <ACB>Haha... I...spent a long time thinking about it\nbefore I landed on that.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_013: You've spent years in those white clothes,\nthe Herald of the Pale Raven.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_014: It just occurred to me you might want to wear a\ndifferent color for a change.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_015: I bought the fabric special and sewed it with my\nown hands. I hope you'll take it.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_016: <NCA>"But...where's yours?"
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_017: Mine? I don't... This is a gift for you.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_018: <NCA>"I think we should match."
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_019: Oh... OK! I would love that.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_020: I don't know if I'm worthy to have matching clothes\nwith the Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_021: But honestly...the idea of it makes me too happy\nto care.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_022: <RSDS>I'll go back and make another cloak. And a couple\nmore things for you! You need sun protection.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_023: Get ready for lots more color too. All the colors of\nthe seasons! Ripe fruit, fallen leaves...
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_024: They'll be comfortable, of course. Don't worry\nabout that.
MID_SE_Ism_Max_S_025: We'll have quite the collection. I'll be so happy for us\nto share that...and our lives together.